{#- The members-library block on the All-Access sales pages.
    Renders entirely from site/_data/library.json off the page's own `lang`.

    This exists because the three All-Access pages hand-wrote the same list and
    all three decayed: on Aug 13, 2026 they were still selling a members area of
    "flexibility, kettlebell, fixing lower back pain" — one deleted that morning,
    two that never existed — while naming none of the eight real entries.
    Shipping a tool is still ONE edit to library.json and every sales page
    updates. Do not hand-write entries back into the pages.

    🚨 CUT FROM SIXTEEN CARDS TO ONE LINE, September 10, 2026 (Iván).
    It had become the members hub copied onto a sales page: sixteen titles, each
    with a paragraph and a Rutina/Herramienta/Guía label, and it was most of the
    reason the page ran 7–12k px. **Nobody buying a subscription reads sixteen
    product descriptions.** Three things are now shown properly further up the
    page — the activation loop, the zones calculator, and a tool you can run
    logged out — and this block is the sentence that says what else is in there.
    *Naming them all still matters; giving each one a card did not.*

    `peekKeys` is the list the page has already shown above; those are skipped
    here so the same tool is not sold twice on one scroll. -#}
{%- set lib = library[lang] or library.es -%}
{%- set order = lib.categoryOrder or ["train", "pain", "numbers"] -%}
{%- set skip = peekKeys or [] -%}
{#- ⚠️ `section--wash` was on this element and computed to `rgba(0,0,0,0)`.
    It is not a typo and not undefined: it is defined in `members.css` and
    `members-dark.css`, and this partial renders on the three PUBLIC All-Access
    pages, which load `all-access.css` and neither of those. A members-area
    class was quietly doing nothing on a sales page.
    🔑 Same family as everything else found this week — `.help a` beating a bare
    `a`, `.cta-final` inheriting a colour that was only right on a light page,
    a rule scoped to `a` missing the sibling that is not one. **A class is only
    a class on a page that loads the sheet defining it**, and nothing in the
    markup says which sheet that is.
    Removed September 10, 2026; the section is white on purpose, which also
    stops it stacking with the wash on `.includes-section` above into one slab.
    ⚠️ If a wash is ever wanted here, define it in `all-access.css`. -#}
<section class="lib-line" id="biblioteca">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>{{ lib.heading }}</h2>
    <p class="section-intro">{{ lib.intro }}</p>
    <dl class="lib-rest">
      {%- for cat in order %}
      {%- set names = [] -%}
      {%- for item in lib.live %}{% if item.category == cat and item.key not in skip %}{% set names = (names.push(item.name), names) %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}
      {%- if names.length %}
      <div>
        <dt>{{ lib.categories[cat] }}</dt>
        <dd>{{ names | join(" · ") }}</dd>
      </div>
      {%- endif %}
      {%- endfor %}
    </dl>
    {%- if lib.soon.length %}
    {#- ⚠️ No `map` filter: Nunjucks is not Jinja2, and it does not have one.
        Same family as the `selectattr` bug in ai-infrastructure §41, which
        silently rendered all 13 cards under all 3 headings. This one at
        least fails loudly. -#}
    <p class="lib-soon-line"><b>{{ lib.soonHeading }}</b> {% for item in lib.soon %}{{ item.name }}{% if not loop.last %} · {% endif %}{% endfor %}</p>
    {%- endif %}
  </div>
</section>
